<figure class="projection-process" data-projection-process>
  <p class="process-kicker">Building the starting signal</p>
  <p class="process-title">From a solver solution to a model-written example</p>
  <ol>
    <li><span class="step-number">01</span><h3>Solver solution</h3><p>An algorithmic solver provides a detailed worked solution.</p></li>
    <li><span class="step-number">02</span><h3>Propose and refine</h3><p>The model writes a response, then makes ten refinements from random cut points. Keep verified answers with a better original-model score.</p></li>
    <li><span class="step-number">03</span><h3>A supervised foothold</h3><p>Train on 256 selected examples for one SFT epoch, then return to RL.</p></li>
  </ol>
  <figcaption>The solver guides the proposal. The score is mean token log probability under the original model on the ordinary puzzle prompt. Verification checks the final assignment; intermediate prose is not certified.</figcaption>
</figure>
